% INVALID certificate: min x s.t. -1 <= x <= 2 has optimum -1, but the lower bound 0 is claimed. The solution s1
% is written as OBJ, which used to alias the objective; reading s2 then erased the objective, so that the empty
% combination D1 proved "0 >= 0".
VER 1.1
VAR 1
x
INT 0
OBJ min
1 0 1
CON 2 0
C1 G -1 1 0 1
C2 L 2 1 0 1
RTP range 0 inf
SOL 2
s1 OBJ
s2 0
DER 1
D1 G 0 OBJ { lin 0 } -1
